ST_Manual.NounManual_1_25_des:
An Anomaly's Wertheimer Index can be estimated based on fluctuations detected in the corresponding area when the Anomaly appears or begins activating its abilities.
The Yggash Court has provided classification standards for evaluating Anomaly ability levels, using the danger levels commonly corresponding to Anomaly ability degrees as examples. The specific classifications are as follows:

Class I - Wertheimer Index fluctuations in the (-2, -1] range, the Anomaly has almost no impact on human social order;
Class II - Wertheimer Index fluctuations in the (-3, -2] range, the Anomaly is capable of causing minor injuries to individuals;
Class III - Wertheimer Index fluctuations in the (-4, -3] range, the Anomaly is capable of causing casualties among individuals;
Class IV - Wertheimer Index fluctuations in the (-5, -4] range, the Anomaly is capable of causing multiple casualties in non-densely populated urban areas;
Class V - Wertheimer Index fluctuations in the (-10, -5] range, the Anomaly is capable of causing mass casualties in urban areas;
Class VI - Wertheimer Index fluctuations in the (-20, -10] range, the Anomaly is capable of causing mass casualties throughout an entire city;
Class VII - Wertheimer Index fluctuations in the (-50, -20] range, the Anomaly is capable of causing an entire city's functions to cease or be destroyed;
Class VIII - Wertheimer Index fluctuations in the (-100, -50] range, the Anomaly is capable of destroying an entire city;
Class IX - Wertheimer Index fluctuations in the (-200, -100] range, the Anomaly is capable of destroying multiple cities;
Class X - Wertheimer Index fluctuations in the (-∞, -200] range, the Anomaly may pose an extinction-level threat to humanity.

Anomaly classes are only used to generally indicate an anomaly's capability range and intensity. The analogies in the classification standards are for reference only; "capable of" does not mean the Anomaly "will definitely cause such consequences."
Since each Anomaly has different characteristics, from a human society perspective, there may exist low-class Anomalies with major hidden dangers, or high-class Anomalies that do not actively harm humans.

ST_Manual.NounManual_1_24_des:
Classifications assigned by the Yggash Court based on the importance or influence of file info, indicating the clearance required to access that file. The specific classifications are as follows:

Public - Info that can be disclosed to all citizens;
Bounty - All members of the Circle can access, including private Anomaly Hunters, organizations, etc.;
Restricted - Members of the Circle's five major public institutions or six major families can access;
Classified - Senior officials of the Circle's five major public institutions or designated personnel can access;
Confidential - Only A6 members are qualified to access.

ST_WorldDescription.SW_Int_Bs_133_002:
1. This manual is issued to ensure the safe and stable operation of the Hethereau rail transit system and proper Anomaly management, and to provide passengers with a secure and reliable travel environment. It is established under the Bureau of Anomaly Control New Containment Safety Protocol and the Hethereau Rail Transit Regulations.
2. All individuals entering any Hethereau Anomaly Express (hereafter "Ghost Train") station—including entrances, platforms, and train cars—must follow these rules. This includes humans, Espers, and Anomalies. Note: For your safety and the safety of others, compliance is mandatory.
3. The Ghost Train operates 24/7 year-round, with the following exceptions:
(1) If a full moon falls on a Wednesday, service is suspended for one day. Stations will be closed from Tuesday 23:30 to Thursday 00:30. Please leave before closure;
(2) If you remain inside after closure, stay calm. Do not panic. Periodically confirm that you are still inside the station, regardless of what you perceive;
(3) Do not use vending machines during closure. If needed, retrieve emergency supplies from beneath the inquiry counter. Do not accept items from other passengers;
(4) Do not enter any train car during closure, even if visible;
(5) After reopening, remain at the inquiry counter until a Train Manager confirms departure. Train Managers appear as semi-transparent owl-like Oddities emitting blue light and wearing a uniform cap with a loudspeaker. Ignore instructions from anyone else.
4. The Bureau of Anomaly Control has upgraded the Ghost Train system using Zerogon Laboratory technology. A "Train Ticket" is no longer required for boarding. If you still possess an outdated ticket:
(1) Do not keep or handle it for extended periods. You may exchange it for an "Outstanding Passenger Certificate" (commemorative only);
(2) Do not destroy it yourself. Submit it to a Train Manager for disposal;
(3) If lost, go to the nearest station, step down the third stair, then retrieve it upon turning back. Do not interact with other tickets until yours is recovered;
(4) If you find a lost ticket, immediately hand it to a Train Manager and follow their instructions;
(5) Only authentic tickets may be used for replacement requests. Forged or borrowed tickets will result in boarding denial.
5. All passengers must undergo security checks by Train Managers. Refusal will result in boarding denial. The following items are prohibited:
(1) Anomalies above Level II not legally contained;
(2) Illegal weapons or containment devices not approved by the BAC;
(3) Hazardous materials including toxins, corrosives, radiation sources, or pathogens;
(4) Any items or Anomalies deemed hazardous to passengers or the train;
(5) Cat-like entities, including feline Oddities (not recommended for transport under any circumstance).
6. When passengers are present, the Ghost Train will arrive within one minute except on shutdown days:
(1) Queue within safety lines and board in order; do not board before others exit. Do not board if doors fail to open or open abnormally;
(2) Car assignments may differ between passengers. Disappearance of other passengers after boarding is normal;
(3) Do not exit through any door that appears mid-transit. Maintain distance until it disappears;
(4) Do not disembark at unannounced stops. If you do, do not attempt to return—seek assistance from a Train Manager;
(5) If a station does not match your expectations, do not exit. Contact a Train Manager immediately.
7. In emergencies, do not use emergency buttons if encountered. The Ghost Train does not have emergency alarm systems. Wait in a safe area. If necessary, Espers may respond without harming other passengers.
8. The following actions are strictly prohibited:
(1) Attempting to contain or nullify the Ghost Train or Train Managers;
(2) Linking external Anomalous Realms to the train system;
(3) Activating high-level Anomaly containment devices onboard;
(4) Using Esper Abilities to disrupt or harm others without emergency justification;
(5) Using alternate transport or teleportation abilities while the train is in motion;
(6) Any other behavior that endangers operations or passengers.
Lost & Found is located at the inquiry counter:
(1) Non-perishable items are kept for up to 6 months;
(2) Anomaly-related devices are transferred to the Bureau of Anomaly Control;
(3) Do not re-enter platforms or trains to retrieve lost items—exit and report to the counter. 
10. Maintain cleanliness and order at all times. Posting, hanging, or marketing activities are prohibited. Continued violations after warning will result in consequences at the passenger's own risk.
Feedback regarding service issues may be submitted to the Bureau of Anomaly Control.
All passengers are expected to follow these rules. Violations may result in service denial. Severe violations may result in outcomes for which the Bureau and Train Managers bear no responsibility.
